Adam Myrow wrote:
> I don't understand why a blue jelly would ever starve. =A0I'd assume that
> a monster that can't move also doesn't need to eat.

The answer just came to me, and its rather simple, really.  Worn
jewelry, including amulets and rings, both consume nutrition of their
own, in addition to whatever your normal hunger rate is.  Even the
ring of slow digestion, which stops natural hunger entirely, does not
eliminate the nutrition drain caused by worn jewelry (including the
nutrition drain from the ring of slow digestion itself).  Thus, any
worn jewelry will slowly deplete the poor blue jelly's nutrition down
to zero, and make it starve.


